assertion  XBD.signal.h.015
anchor     basedefs/signal.h.html#DESCRIPTION/SIG_BLOCK
class      required
since      1988
says       <signal.h> defines SIG_BLOCK, SIG_UNBLOCK and SIG_SETMASK as
           integer constant expressions with different values.
note       That the values are distinct is inferred from their having to
           be told apart, not stated (Q-55).
test       t/015-sig-block.c
nomutant   compile-time check; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.signal.h.016
anchor     basedefs/signal.h.html#DESCRIPTION/SA_NOCLDSTOP
class      disputed
since      2008
says       <signal.h> defines SA_NOCLDSTOP, SA_RESETHAND, SA_RESTART, SA_SIGINFO
           and SA_NODEFER as non-zero constants with no bits in common, so
           any of them can be combined in sa_flags.
note       disputed (Q-55): <signal.h> calls these symbolic constants
           and sigaction() speaks of flags set in sa_flags, but nothing
           says they are non-zero with no bits in common; a FAIL is
           logged as INSPECT. sigaction() lets these flags be set in
           sa_flags together, which needs each to be a non-zero value
           with no bits in common with the others.
test       t/016-sa-flags.c
nomutant   compile-time check; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.signal.h.017
anchor     basedefs/signal.h.html#DESCRIPTION/SA_ONSTACK
class      disputed
when       XSI
since      2001
says       On XSI systems <signal.h> also defines SA_ONSTACK and SA_NOCLDWAIT,
           non-zero, with no bits in common with each other or the other SA_
           flags.
uses       XBD.signal.h.016
note       disputed (Q-55): <signal.h> calls these symbolic constants
           and sigaction() speaks of flags set in sa_flags, but nothing
           says they are non-zero with no bits in common; a FAIL is
           logged as INSPECT. SA_NOCLDWAIT is still XSI-shaded although
           its CHANGE HISTORY says it moved to the Base (standard issue
           SI-10); this follows the shading.
test       t/017-sa-flags-xsi.c
nomutant   compile-time check; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.signal.h.018
anchor     basedefs/signal.h.html#DESCRIPTION/SS_ONSTACK
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      2001
says       On XSI systems <signal.h> defines SS_ONSTACK and SS_DISABLE with
           different values, and MINSIGSTKSZ and SIGSTKSZ with positive
           values, all four as integer constant expressions.
note       XBD 3 defines a symbolic constant as an object-like macro
           expanding to an integer constant expression unless stated
           otherwise; <signal.h> states no exception for these four.
test       t/018-altstack.c
nomutant   compile-time check; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

